title Historical revision Comparison View

participant User
participant ComparisonView
participant ServerApiClient
participant ResourceRevisionAPI
participant Authorization
participant ResourceRepository
participant ResourceDiff
participant DiagramViewport

User -> ComparisonView: Select base and target revisions
ComparisonView -> ServerApiClient: listResourceRevisions(projectId, contextId, resourceId)
ServerApiClient -> ResourceRevisionAPI: GET revision summaries
ResourceRevisionAPI -> Authorization: authorize resource:read in context
Authorization --> ResourceRevisionAPI: Allow or deny
ResourceRevisionAPI -> ResourceRepository: Read summaries for exact resource lineage
ResourceRepository --> ResourceRevisionAPI: Revision identities and metadata
ResourceRevisionAPI --> ServerApiClient: Revision summaries
ServerApiClient --> ComparisonView: Candidate revision selectors

ComparisonView -> ServerApiClient: getResourceRevision(baseRevision)
ComparisonView -> ServerApiClient: getResourceRevision(targetRevision)
ServerApiClient -> ResourceRevisionAPI: Read each requested snapshot
ResourceRevisionAPI -> Authorization: Re-authorize resource:read
Authorization --> ResourceRevisionAPI: Allow or deny
ResourceRevisionAPI -> ResourceRepository: Load immutable snapshots
ResourceRepository --> ResourceRevisionAPI: Snapshot content, type, authorship, time
ResourceRevisionAPI --> ServerApiClient: Snapshot responses
ServerApiClient --> ComparisonView: Responses or unavailable error
ComparisonView -> ComparisonView: Verify project, context, resource, revision, representation
ComparisonView -> ResourceDiff: Compare same-type Conceptual or Database snapshots
ResourceDiff --> ComparisonView: Changes with match basis, source evidence, diagnostics, limits
ComparisonView -> DiagramViewport: Render each verified snapshot with independent camera
ComparisonView --> User: Difference list, detail, evidence, fallback or access error

note over ComparisonView : Mismatched identity rejects the pair. Responses from an obsolete pair are ignored and protected pane content is cleared.
note over ResourceDiff : Cross-type pairs use textual evidence only. Heuristic/name correspondence stays a candidate, never a confirmed rename.
